# leakscan path allowances — root-relative globs.
# site/vendor/ holds pinned, unmodified third-party bytes (ADR
# 2026-08-08-0450, ADR 2026-08-08-0546) — minified/bundled JS and CSS,
# not content this repo authored. Their packed literal tables (colour
# tables, projection constants, test fixture coordinates baked into the
# library) read as ipv4/coordinate/phone/payment-card shapes to a
# structural scanner; none of it is this repo's personal or estate
# data. tools/vendor_check.py is what actually guards this directory
# (a sha256 pin per file, checked every run), so leaving it in scope
# here would only ever produce noise, never signal.
site/vendor/**

# tools/vendor-manifest.json's entire content is npm integrity hashes
# (sha512, base64) and per-file sha256 pins — long structured digit/hex
# runs that read as ipv4/phone-shaped data to a structural scanner, and
# every future re-vendor adds more of them. The real guard on this file
# is vendor_check.py's exact-value comparison, not a shape scan.
tools/vendor-manifest.json
